Key Concepts Learned

Network Discovery
Network discovery is the process of identifying systems connected to a network and collecting information about them.

Ports
Ports allow network-enabled applications and services to communicate. Identifying active ports helps security professionals understand how a system interacts with other devices.

Services
Services provide specific functionality on a system. Discovering active services helps build a picture of a system's purpose and potential attack surface.

Key Learning Outcomes
During this lab session, I gained practical experience using Nmap to perform network discovery and service identification. I learned how systems expose services through ports and how security professionals gather information during the reconnaissance phase of an assessment.

Reflection
Today I completed my first network discovery exercise using Nmap. This allowed me to observe how systems expose services across a network and understand the importance of identifying active communication channels before performing further analysis or security assessments.
